build.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Master has now opened up for =
3.3 development and patches are merging.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Dunfell has seen a number of =
CVE report improvements (count of 202 down to 71 in the past three =
months), either through patches/upgrades or in corrections to the CVE =
database information, thanks Steve and all those who&#8217;ve =
helped.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The dunfell CVE improvements =
have also drastically improved the situation with =
master.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo11;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur. You can see the list of failures we&#8217;re =
continuing to see by searching for the &#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in =
bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The SWAT team has been =
re-established. A new mailing has been created as <a =
href=3D"mailto:swat@lists.yoctoproject.org"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>swat@lists.yoctoproject.org</span></a> to =
support this and a number of member organizations have agreed to help =
staff this team. We are in the process of getting the process running =
again and in due course there will be the option of other community =
members being able to help too. The tools and processes are under review =
to allow us to optimise the process. Thanks to the members and everyone =
participating to make this happen!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are big improvements =
underway to the autobuilder display of builds, for example, <a =
href=3D"https://autobuilder.yoctoproject.org/typhoon/#/builders/44/builds=
/2744"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://autobuilder.yoctoproject.org/typhoon/#/bu=
ilders/44/builds/2744</span></a> which shows many more individual steps =
with more detailed information. There still needs to be improvements to =
the configuration markup to make best use of this (help welcome!) but =
this should significantly improve the autobuilder =
readability.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo12;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are other ideas being =
discussed around autobuilder usability improvements such as remembering =
field history (patch submitted to upstream buildbot), better =
success/failure count reporting and potential replacement of the =
buildlog wiki page and autobuilder integration with a specific purpose =
django app.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
